# Keep line endings deterministic across checkouts.
#
# The machine .toml files are embedded byte-for-byte into the binary by
# cmake/embed_machines.cmake (as a raw unsigned-char array, HEX-read). A Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite them CRLF and change the embedded
# bytes -- so pin all text to LF, and mark the binary media so git never touches it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.toml text eol=lf
*.exp  text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# .bat files are Windows-only and only ever run by cmd.exe. Store them CRLF so a
# checkout matches the platform they belong to -- the native convention there, and the
# one line ending cmd.exe is guaranteed to parse without surprises around labels/goto.
*.bat  text eol=crlf

# CP/M source and listing files (.ASM, .PRN, .INC, .Z80, .LST) go onto a CP/M disk as they
# are: pasted with PIP x=CON:, run through the assembler's LOAD, or carried in a bootable
# image. CP/M needs CRLF line ends in them (and, for text, a trailing ^Z). The global
# `eol=lf` rule above would strip the CRs on checkout, which broke `PIP R.ASM=CON:`: the
# pasted source arrived as one line with no line ends, so ASM produced nothing (issue #118).
#
#   -text                 Git never changes a line end. The repository and the working
#                         tree both hold CRLF.
#   diff                  `git diff` shows these files as text. (`binary` would turn
#                         this off.)
#   whitespace=cr-at-eol  `git diff` does not mark the CR at the end of a line.
#
# Keep every one of these files CRLF on all lines. (.HEX is binary in the media section below.)
*.ASM -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.asm -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.PRN -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.prn -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.INC -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.inc -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.Z80 -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.z80 -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.LST -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.lst -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol

# The CP/M symbol-file fixtures carry two more format-under-test extensions
# (tests/programs/symbols/README.md): their CRLF and trailing ^Z padding are part of the
# format, so they follow the same rule. (.ASM/.PRN there are covered by the rule above.)
tests/programs/symbols/*.SYM -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
tests/programs/symbols/*.MAC -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol

# The CPU exerciser sources (tests/cpu/*.MAC) are the same kind of period CP/M file as the
# .ASM files above: fetched from altairclone.com (see tests/cpu/PROVENANCE.md), CRLF and all.
# The .COM images they assemble to are the binary media that actually run the gate.
tests/cpu/*.MAC -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol

# The MBL boot ROM's source and listing are deramp originals, CRLF like every other
# CP/M file here (roms/MBL/). (.HEX is binary globally below.)
roms/MBL/*.PRN -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
roms/MBL/*.ASM -text diff whitespace=cr-at-eol

# Period media and disk images are binary -- never munge.
*.DSK binary
*.dsk binary
*.bin binary
*.BIN binary
*.hex binary
*.HEX binary
*.keys binary
*.tap binary
*.TAP binary
*.wav binary
*.WAV binary
*.pdf binary
*.PDF binary
